Fix heap overflow added by t1lib-5.1.2-segfault.patch: intT1_GetFileSearchPath()
unconditionally wrote a NUL at offset 900 of the malloc'ed search path string,
past the end of any path shorter than that. It is called once per entry of a
FontDataBase, so a database with ~25 fonts corrupts the heap at T1_InitLib()
("malloc(): unsorted double linked list corrupted"). Only truncate long paths.

Index: t1lib-5.1.2/lib/t1lib/t1env.c
===================================================================
--- t1lib-5.1.2.orig/lib/t1lib/t1env.c
+++ t1lib-5.1.2/lib/t1lib/t1env.c
@@ -824,7 +824,8 @@ char *T1_GetFileSearchPath( int type)
 char *intT1_GetFileSearchPath( int type)
 {
    char  *res = T1_GetFileSearchPath(type);
-   res[900] = 0;
+   if (res != NULL && strlen(res) > 900)
+      res[900] = 0;
    return res;
 }
 
